messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI agents enter mainstream office and knowledge work.",
      "detail": "Large language model agents begin handling complex software, legal, and administrative tasks. Productivity rises, but displacement starts in junior white-collar roles."
    },
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "Global CO2 emissions peak.",
      "detail": "Coal declines faster than expected in China and India, while solar, wind, and batteries dominate new capacity additions. This marks the beginning of a long emissions plateau and decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "A major AI-generated election crisis occurs.",
      "detail": "Hyper-realistic synthetic media disrupts a G20 election and makes attribution difficult. Emergency rules on political deepfakes follow in several countries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Renewables provide more than half of global electricity.",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, hydro, and nuclear become the dominant electricity sources. Fossil fuels begin a structural decline in power generation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "First crewed Mars orbital mission returns safely.",
      "detail": "A government-commercial partnership sends astronauts around Mars and back, proving long-duration deep-space life support and radiation shielding."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "Cultured meat reaches cost parity with conventional meat.",
      "detail": "Lab-grown and fermentation-derived proteins become cheaper than industrial livestock in many markets. Agricultural emissions and land use begin to fall."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "First human landing on Mars.",
      "detail": "A crewed mission lands on Mars and returns safely. The landing site remains a temporary research outpost, not yet a permanent colony."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "AI-designed antibiotics reach clinical use.",
      "detail": "New AI-discovered antibiotics and antivirals enter the market and begin reversing some antimicrobial resistance trends."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Global population reaches about 9.1 billion.",
      "detail": "Population growth slows as most countries fall below replacement fertility. Aging accelerates in East Asia and Europe, while Africa still grows."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "Autonomous weapons are used in a regional conflict.",
      "detail": "Loitering drones and AI targeting systems fight with limited human oversight. The incident prompts partial international restrictions on autonomous lethal systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2043,
      "event": "First commercial fusion power plant begins operation.",
      "detail": "A net-energy fusion reactor supplies electricity to a national grid. Initial costs remain high, but the technology is proven."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "A global AI governance treaty is signed.",
      "detail": "After a near-catastrophic AI failure in financial or military systems, major powers agree on licensing, testing, and emergency kill-switch standards."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces restore movement and sight.",
      "detail": "Implanted neural interfaces allow paralyzed people to walk and blind people to perceive shapes. Consumer neurotechnology remains limited and regulated."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global warming reaches about 1.8 degrees Celsius above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Despite declining emissions, committed warming and slow decarbonization in heavy industry and transport keep global temperature rising for now."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Human-level AI is deployed in controlled domains.",
      "detail": "AI systems match humans on many broad cognitive benchmarks. They are not autonomous general agents but operate under strict safeguards and human supervision."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Large-scale carbon dioxide removal begins.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture and enhanced weathering remove billions of tons of CO2 per year. Carbon taxes and climate reparations fund much of the effort."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Life expectancy in wealthy countries reaches 90 to 100.",
      "detail": "Senolytics, gene therapy, and continuous health monitoring slow aging. Access to these treatments remains unequal."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "A permanent lunar research station is established.",
      "detail": "A multinational station at the lunar south pole supports science, water extraction, and fuel production for deep-space missions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "AI manages most complex infrastructure.",
      "detail": "Energy grids, transport, water, and supply chains are run by AI with human oversight. Efficiency improves, but cyber-risks become a central security concern."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Global population peaks near 10.3 billion.",
      "detail": "Africa remains the main growth region while many other regions decline. After the peak, global population begins a slow long-term decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Sea levels rise by about 0.6 meters.",
      "detail": "Major coastal cities invest heavily in barriers and managed retreat. Low-lying island nations face severe land loss and displacement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Net-zero global emissions are achieved.",
      "detail": "Global emissions reach net-zero or slightly negative. Warming stabilizes around 2.0 to 2.4 degrees Celsius above preindustrial."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Ecosystem restoration uses gene-edited species.",
      "detail": "Coral, wetlands, and forests are restored with species engineered for heat tolerance and disease resistance. Biodiversity recovery begins, though ecosystems are not identical to past ones."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Asteroid mining begins for platinum-group metals.",
      "detail": "Robotic missions capture and process near-Earth asteroids. Space-based manufacturing grows, reducing some mining pressure on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "The Mars settlement reaches 100,000 people.",
      "detail": "The colony is mostly self-sufficient in water, food, and basic materials. Population grows through local births and continuing immigration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Space-based solar power contributes to Earth's grid.",
      "detail": "Orbiting solar arrays beam power to Earth and to space habitats. Fusion and space solar power provide much of the energy used in the inner solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "First interstellar probe returns data from Alpha Centauri.",
      "detail": "A laser-sail or fusion-driven probe launched decades earlier sends back images and measurements of nearby exoplanets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Genetic divergence of space populations begins.",
      "detail": "Humans on Mars, the Moon, and orbital habitats show early signs of adaptation to low gravity and radiation environments. These changes are minor but measurable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Earth's climate and biodiversity largely stabilize.",
      "detail": "CO2 is near preindustrial levels after centuries of removal. Ecosystems recover, though species composition is permanently changed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Human cognition is enhanced through neural interfaces.",
      "detail": "Many people use memory prostheses and direct brain-to-AI communication. Societies debate the boundaries of human identity."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Solar system population reaches several million.",
      "detail": "Permanent habitats exist from Mercury orbit to the outer moons. Earth remains the cultural and political center of the solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "First interstellar generation ship is launched.",
      "detail": "A slow multi-century mission heads toward a nearby habitable exoplanet, carrying a self-sustaining population."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "First permanent settlement is established around another star.",
      "detail": "A robotic precursor confirmed a habitable target, and a later wave of colonists or embryos establishes a small extrasolar colony."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Human-derived intelligences inhabit multiple star systems.",
      "detail": "Biological humans, augmented humans, and AI descendants live in several systems. Light-speed communication delays keep them largely independent."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Dyson swarm construction begins around the Sun.",
      "detail": "Vast solar collectors and habitats form an incomplete shell, supplying energy for large-scale computation and propulsion."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Major post-biological speciation occurs.",
      "detail": "Most human-descended intelligences are now non-biological or hybrid. Biological Homo sapiens persists in protected Earth habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth enters a managed state.",
      "detail": "Earth's ecosystems, climate, and geology are deliberately managed by post-human intelligences to preserve complexity and historical value."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human-descended intelligence spans dozens of star systems.",
      "detail": "No faster-than-light travel has been invented, but slow expansion continues. Earth is a historical and ecological reserve, and some populations still identify as human."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity most likely survives and spreads slowly through the solar system and nearby stars, but undergoes genetic, cognitive, and cultural changes that make 'human' a broader category. The main risks are concentrated in the next few centuries from AI, engineered pathogens, and climate disruption. By 10000, human-descended intelligence is likely to be widely distributed but still constrained by light-speed communication."
}
